Descriptive only (not gated): per-task max run + span; timeouts; first ok edit time (agent-clock s); edit_missing_param and cmd_error_shell
counts (trace_tool_errors.py totals); agent clock sum; per-id patch bytes D -> F; exact sign test on empty discordants; gates a/b/d/e.
Honest limits: n=8/k=1 is a mechanism screen, not quality evidence. Temperature 0.2 is itself stochastic, so arm D's loops may not recur
at 0.2 on a re-run either; a LOOP-REDUCED verdict can't separate the temperature effect from run-to-run noise. An empty-diff count is not
a pass rate. Temperature can change fix quality invisibly, so 0.6 can only enter plan 007 as a paired arm and can't ship on this screen.
