ops/codex/ask-20261106T021410.md:17:**Does it load bundle Python? Yes, as sandboxed skill scripts; no, as arbitrary agent/tool/callback modules.** Skill directories are loaded and attached to a `SkillToolset` with the harness executor. For `.py` scripts, ADK materializes the bundled source and executes it with `runpy.run_path`. See [resolvers/tools.py:213](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/adk_submission/resolvers/tools.py:213), [resolvers/tools.py:253](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/adk_submission/resolvers/tools.py:253), and [skill_toolset.py:1359](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/google/adk/tools/skill_toolset.py:1359).
ops/codex/ask-20261106T021410.md:23:The restricted `AgentToolRef` accepts only `config_path` and `skip_summarization`; unknown fields are forbidden. The LLM agent schema likewise has no separate call, turn, or time budget. Compilation constructs `AgentTool(agent=..., skip_summarization=...)` without a budget argument. See [schema.py:95](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/adk_submission/schema.py:95), [schema.py:247](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/adk_submission/schema.py:247), [schema.py:277](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/adk_submission/schema.py:277), and [resolvers/tools.py:115](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/adk_submission/resolvers/tools.py:115).
ops/codex/ask-20261106T021410.md:27:- **Separate cap:** ADK exposes `max_llm_calls` through `RunConfig`. Its `AgentTool` inherits the caller’s run configuration; the nested invocation has its own counter against that inherited ceiling. This is **not a smaller analyzer-specific allowance configurable here**. See [run_config.py:271](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/google/adk/agents/run_config.py:271) and [agent_tool.py:320](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/google/adk/tools/agent_tool.py:320).
ops/codex/ask-20261106T021410.md:28:- **Time accounting:** analyzer inference and tools execute inside the root’s enclosing session timeout. They consume the same `max_time_minutes`; there is no reserved root-edit interval. See [agent_runner.py:718](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/harness/agent_runner.py:718) and [agent_runner.py:783](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/harness/agent_runner.py:783).
ops/codex/ask-20261106T021410.md:29:- **Tool accounting:** analyzer calls to registered harness tools consume the shared `max_tool_calls`. Both agents receive tools bound to the same context, and the budget decorator checks/increments that context. **The outer `agent_tool` invocation itself is not an additional harness-tool debit.** See [agent_runner.py:601](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/harness/agent_runner.py:601), [resolvers/tools.py:64](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/adk_submission/resolvers/tools.py:64), [base.py:86](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/tools/base.py:86), and [context.py:549](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/context.py:549).
ops/codex/ask-20261106T021410.md:37:A checkpoint script can accept replacement arguments, check the live diff, and apply a validated source edit. `run_skill_script` receives script arguments and invokes the executor only when called. See [skill_toolset.py:1887](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/google/adk/tools/skill_toolset.py:1887) and [skill_toolset.py:2058](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/google/adk/tools/skill_toolset.py:2058).
ops/codex/ask-20261106T021410.md:39:There is **no usable bundle callback for call N or deadline proximity**. Although callback-name fields exist, the harness passes no callback registry. The resolver immediately returns `{}` when that registry is `None`; declaring callback names therefore installs nothing. See [agent_runner.py:616](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/harness/agent_runner.py:616) and [callbacks.py:83](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/adk_submission/resolvers/callbacks.py:83).
ops/codex/ask-20261106T021410.md:47:See [execution.py:132](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/tools/execution.py:132) and [base.py:47](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/tools/base.py:47).
ops/codex/ask-20261106T021410.md:57:**Its patch fields describe the submitted snapshot, not current workspace modifications.** Before submission, `patch_size=0` can coexist with a valid live source diff. It supplies no changed-file list, source classification, or remaining-turn count. See [execution.py:119](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/tools/execution.py:119).
ops/codex/ask-20261106T021410.md:59:Both `get_status` and `submit_patch` are exempt from counted tool calls, although their budget wrapper still checks elapsed time. See [execution.py:76](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/tools/execution.py:76), [execution.py:119](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/tools/execution.py:119), and [context.py:527](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/context.py:527).
ops/codex/ask-20261106T021410.md:61:`submit_patch` obtains the diff, strips protected files, then **unconditionally stores the result and sets `patch_submitted=True`**. Empty results—including a diff emptied by stripping tests—are accepted. That flag disables fallback collection. See [execution.py:97](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/tools/execution.py:97) and [agent_runner.py:1054](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/harness/agent_runner.py:1054).
ops/codex/ask-20261106T021410.md:63:A skill can refuse its **own preflight**, but cannot prevent the model from calling the separately exposed `submit_patch`. Removing `submit_patch` from every agent’s tools is expressible and prevents premature snapshot capture, but still cannot create a missing edit. Tool exposure comes from each agent’s declared list: [llm.py:62](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/adk_submission/builders/llm.py:62).
ops/codex/ask-20261106T021410.md:73:This requests termination at 15 seconds and forced termination one second later. The Docker backend itself uses `timeout`, establishing its availability there. The harness also automatically reduces command timeouts near the session deadline. See [execution.py:148](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/tools/execution.py:148), [docker.py:703](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/sandbox/docker.py:703), and [execution.py:31](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/tools/execution.py:31).
ops/codex/ask-20261106T021410.md:75:**Another numeric total-output cap per turn: NOT FEASIBLE.** `max_output_tokens` is the supported total generation limit. `thinking_budget` is separately expressible and forwarded as a thinking-specific backend setting; it is not another total-output cap. Stop sequences can terminate generation but provide no numeric bound. See [schema.py:202](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/adk_submission/schema.py:202) and [generation.py:434](/home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/adk_submission/resolvers/generation.py:434).
